# ML DataMind Sustainable Use License: Draft v0.2

> **Draft — pending legal review.** This text has not been reviewed by a
> lawyer. It states, in plain language, how the ML DataMind project wants its
> code to be used. It must be reviewed by qualified legal counsel before it is
> treated as final.
>
> **Source available, not open source.** This license is not approved by the
> Open Source Initiative and does not meet the Open Source Definition, because
> it limits some commercial uses (section 4).
>
> **Which versions this covers.** This license applies from the commit that adds
> it, onward. Earlier versions of ML DataMind (through commit `d4875a8`, version
> 0.1.0, published 29 September to 13 October 2026) stay under the MIT License,
> which is preserved in [`LICENSE-MIT`](LICENSE-MIT). See section 9.

## In short

**Free, no commercial license needed:** read, study, clone, modify, adapt and
extend ML DataMind; keep private forks; use it internally in a company,
university, municipality or transit operator; research and education;
consulting and implementation; integrations; generating, publishing and selling
GTFS feeds, datasets, reports and other Output; and building apps that consume
that Output.

**Commercial license needed:** only to offer ML DataMind itself, or a fork or
substantial modification of it, to others as a product or service: SaaS or a
hosted service, giving Third Parties access to its functionality (including on
demand through another app or service), resale, white-label, or using it as the
core of a product that competes directly with it.

Writing your own system from scratch, with your own code, is never restricted.

Copyright (c) 2026 Josué Arcos and Jhair Jiménez (the "Licensor").

## 1. Definitions

- **"Software"**: ML DataMind, meaning the source code, documentation,
  configuration and other materials in this repository that carry this license,
  together with any modifications you make to them.
- **"You"**: the person or organization using the Software.
- **"Organization"**: any legal entity, including a company, university, public
  body, municipality, transit operator, non-profit or research group.
- **"Output"**: the data, files and reports produced by running the Software,
  such as GTFS feeds, route and stop datasets, and audit reports. Output is not
  part of the Software.
- **"Third Party"**: anyone other than You, your own Organization and the people
  who work for it or for you under contract.
- **"Hosted Offering"**: making the functionality of the Software available to
  Third Parties as a service, instance, platform, API or subscription, whether
  or not a fee is charged. Delivering Output to a Third Party is not a Hosted
  Offering. Letting a Third Party run or use the Software is, including by
  invoking its functionality on demand, directly or indirectly, through another
  application or service.
- **"Modified Version"**: the Software as modified, adapted or extended by
  anyone, including a private fork.
- **"Engine"**: the parts of the Software that reconstruct routes and stops,
  name routes with evidence, and generate GTFS (the five-phase pipeline).

## 2. Grant

Subject to this license, the Licensor grants You a worldwide, royalty-free,
non-exclusive license to use, copy, modify, create derivative works of and
distribute the Software, for the permitted uses in section 3 and under the
conditions in section 5. Nothing in this license lets You do what section 4
restricts without a commercial license.

## 3. Permitted uses

You may:

1. **Study** the code and learn from it.
2. Use it for **personal** purposes, hobby projects and experiments.
3. Use it for **research and education**, including at universities, and
   publish papers, theses and teaching material about it.
4. Use it **inside an Organization**, commercial or not, to process the data the
   Organization owns or is entrusted with, including data of its clients. This
   includes companies, municipal and other government bodies, transit operators
   and consultancies. People working for the Organization under contract may
   operate it on the Organization's behalf. An application inside the
   Organization may invoke the Software live for the Organization's own
   internal users (its people and those working for it under contract).
5. **Produce, use, share, publish and sell Output**, subject to the licenses of
   the underlying data (for example OpenStreetMap's ODbL). You may also build,
   offer and sell applications, services and products that use or consume
   Output, such as a trip-planning app that reads GTFS feeds produced with the
   Software. Using Output does not make an application a competitor of ML
   DataMind.
6. Offer **professional services** around the Software, such as consulting,
   training, implementation, customization and integration work, and charge for
   your time and expertise, including running the Software to process a
   client's data and delivering the resulting Output (see the example below).
   You may not charge for the Software itself or for access to it (section 4).
7. Build and share **integrations**: connectors, plugins, scripts and tools that
   work with the Software through its documented interfaces (its database
   schema, file formats and MCP server, for example) and do not include a
   substantial part of the Software. Those works are yours and may carry any
   license you choose.
8. **Contribute** improvements to the project (see `CONTRIBUTING.md`).
9. **Share copies** of the Software, modified or not, free of charge and under
   this license, as section 5 describes.
10. **Modify, adapt, extend and keep private forks.** Any person or
    Organization may modify, adapt and extend the Software, maintain private
    forks of it, and use those Modified Versions internally, as in items 2 to 4.
    This needs no commercial license, and You are not required to publish Your
    modifications.

**Example: a consultancy.** A consultancy may run the Software to process a
client's data, charge for that work, and deliver GTFS feeds, datasets, reports
and other Output to the client, without a commercial license. It may also
install and configure the Software on the client's own systems for the client's
internal use, charging for its time and not for the Software. It needs a
commercial license only if it gives the client hosted access to the Software,
sells access to ML DataMind itself, or turns it into a SaaS, white-label or
resale offering.

## 4. Uses that need a commercial license

A commercial license is needed only to offer ML DataMind itself, or a fork or
substantial modification of it, to others as a product or service. Using it,
modifying it and keeping forks inside Your Organization never needs one. Unless
You hold a written commercial license from the Licensor, You may not:

1. **Run a Hosted Offering or give access to it**: offer ML DataMind to Third
   Parties as "ML DataMind as a Service", a hosted or managed instance, a
   platform or an API, or otherwise let Third Parties use the functionality of
   the Software, directly or indirectly, including through another application
   or service.
2. **Resell or white-label it**: sell, resell, license, sublicense or rent the
   Software or access to it, including under a white-label, OEM or rebranded
   arrangement.
3. **Commercialize a fork**: offer, sell or distribute the Software, a fork of
   it, or a substantially modified version of it, as a commercial product or
   service, or as part of one, for a fee.
4. **Build a competing product on it**: use the Software, its code, or a
   Modified Version whose Engine substantially modifies the Software's Engine,
   as the core of a software product or platform that competes directly with ML
   DataMind. A product competes directly when it gives Third Parties the same
   kind of capability as ML DataMind (reconstructing routes and stops, naming
   routes with evidence, generating GTFS) as a tool or platform, rather than by
   delivering Output or professional services.

**Applications and services built around the Software.**

- An application that consumes GTFS feeds, datasets or other Output already
  generated with the Software is permitted.
- An application inside an Organization may invoke the Software live for that
  Organization's own internal users.
- If an application or service lets customers or other external users invoke
  the functionality of the Software on demand, directly or indirectly, that is a
  Hosted Offering and needs a commercial license.

These restrictions are about reusing, deriving from or commercializing the
Software or a substantial modification of its code. They do **not** restrict:

- creating, from scratch, another system that does something similar, even one
  that competes with ML DataMind, as long as it uses Your own code;
- using, selling or distributing Output, or building applications, services and
  products that consume Output (section 3.5);
- consulting, implementation and other professional services (section 3.6);
- integrations, connectors and plugins that work with the Software through its
  documented interfaces without including a substantial part of it
  (section 3.7);
- using the Software's documented interfaces inside Your own Organization;
- knowledge, techniques or ideas learned from using or studying the Software;
- modifying the Software and keeping private forks for internal use
  (section 3.10).

## 5. Conditions for sharing copies

Using the Software and keeping Your modifications inside Your Organization is
not "sharing", and You are not required to publish them. If You share the
Software or a Modified Version with anyone outside Your Organization:

- do it free of charge;
- include this license, the copyright notice and the `LICENSE-MIT` file for the
  earlier versions;
- mark the files you changed;
- do not remove or hide notices, and do not say or suggest that your version is
  the official one or that the Licensor endorses it.

Everyone who receives a copy from You receives a license from the Licensor on
these same terms.

## 6. Names and marks

This license grants no rights to the names "ML DataMind" or "DataMind", to their
logos, or to any other marks of the Licensor. You may use the name to state
honestly where your work comes from or that it works with ML DataMind, for
example "based on the ML DataMind source" or "works with ML DataMind".

## 7. Third-party components and data

Third-party components, libraries, tools and data keep their own licenses, and
this license grants no rights in them. Published GTFS datasets are licensed
separately by their own data license (the Open Database License 1.0 for the
datasets published by the project) and are not covered by this license.

## 8. Commercial licenses

The Licensor may grant separate written licenses for the uses in section 4, on
terms agreed case by case. To ask for one, write to
josuearcos1307@gmail.com or see [`docs/COMMERCIAL-LICENSING.md`](docs/COMMERCIAL-LICENSING.md).

## 9. Earlier versions

Versions of the Software published before this license took effect remain
available under the license that applied when they were published. This license
does not take back or change any right granted for them. See
[`docs/legal/VERSIONS-AND-LICENSES.md`](docs/legal/VERSIONS-AND-LICENSES.md).

## 10. Ending of rights

If You break section 4 or section 5, your rights under this license end
automatically. If it was your first breach and You fully correct it within 30
days after the Licensor notifies You in writing, your rights are restored.
Ending your rights under this license does not affect rights You hold under a
license to an earlier version or under a separate commercial license.

## 11. No warranty and limit of liability

The Software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular
purpose and non-infringement. To the extent the law allows, the Licensor is not
liable for any claim, damages or other liability arising from the Software or
from its use.

## 12. General

If part of this license is found unenforceable, the rest stays in force. Not
enforcing a term at one time does not waive it later.

Governing law and venue: **[TO BE DEFINED WITH LEGAL COUNSEL]**.
